# Reactions in the lanes — who answers a knock, a power taken and a power run out, and what they remember
# A design, and a trial in the game (the reactions switch, off for everyone). Every deed is a candidate for the maker: keep, change or strike each row.
#>lore_land_surfaces_reactions_in_the_lanes
#:surface #!proposal
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!semantics

~<rationale>{
  The lanes had seven places where a face came up beside them, each with one of a few short words, and nothing at all when a kept light or a borrowed slowness ran out. Whoever carried the pie took every knock the same way. The people of the lanes already have moods, knacks and things they remember; this lets those show at the moments play turns on, so a reader wonders why the clown is glad of a knock or what the clerk is writing. Nobody is given a line to say: a reaction is a face, a mood, and a deed told by the narrator.
}

^"grounded_in"{
  panel: "pie-game.mjs meanwhile: a portrait beside the lanes, in one of five moods"
  remembers: "characters.mjs REMEMBERS: what each remembers of the reader, counted from the deeds every carried chapter keeps; shown on the portrait sheet and, until now, nowhere in the lanes"
  no_words: "cadences.spw: no character is given words; sound-and-voice.spw asks whether anyone in the lanes should speak, and it is still open"
  pacing: "pie-pacing.mjs: a beat offered is released, merged or folded, never lost"
}

^"moments"{
  taken: "a power taken, by the word it does longest: take:lit, take:lag, take:unkept, take:warm, take:fed, take:glimpse, take:true_aim, then its charges, its acts and what it feeds"
  run_out: "a timed power running out: end:lit, end:lag, end:unkept, end:warm, end:fed, end:glimpse, end:true_aim. Before this, a power ended with nothing said"
  knock: "a knock, one moment for each thing the road can knock with"
  gift: "gift:mine, gift:finger_heart, gift:hi_bear and gift:rival: on a stream (pie-live.mjs, ?live) the lanes answer what is sent, someone standing first; a gift to the other side is answered by Mr. BaneWAP accepting it on their behalf"
  story: "story:boon and story:bane: a passage going by that leans one way is answered by someone who leans with it (pie-story-lane.mjs)"
  table: ~"book/scripts/home/pie-reactions.mjs"
  size: "48 moments and 83 rows on 2026-11-13; reactions:check holds every knock, timed power and spell word to an answer for each of the five carriers"
}

^"who_answers"{
  order: "someone standing in the lanes, then the carrier in their own row, then whoever carries, then anyone"
  telling: "a row for the first time, for a repeat, or for a reader the lanes have answered five times before comes ahead of a row for any telling, so a second knock is not the first one said again"
  shown: "a face in the meanwhile panel, in the row's mood, and the deed in the caption, paced like any other beat; the deed is said the first two times a carry, and after that the face is enough"
  figure: "the figure answers with a mood and no deed: it has no interior to tell"
}

^"the_other_way"{
  clown: "a clown carrying the pie is glad of a knock, and counts it as a WAP that went the wrong way"
  mime: "a mime standing by its struck wall does not move"
  porter: "the porter barely notes a second knock; storms weigh more"
  clerk: "the clerk, knocked by a clerk, writes a slip for the clerk"
}

^"remembered"{
  when: "once a carry, when someone first comes into the lanes: Boof, BoonWAP holding court, BaneWAP announcing, a clown, a mime, a clerk"
  what: "the line characters.mjs already holds for them, with the count from earlier carries"
  nothing_yet: "the Genie, the porter and the figure have no line: nothing they remember is written"
}

!guards[
  "A deed is narration: no quotation marks, no first person, at most 84 characters"
  "Nobody speaks, and the mimes stay silent: their rows are hands, gloves and a wall"
  "The figure is never named and is given no deed; the hat and the Egg are in no row"
  "No row scolds the reader, and none is about a child"
  "A reaction changes nothing in play: it is seen and read, never scored"
]

?open[
  "Which rows stay: every deed here is a candidate"
  "With reactions on, a knock no longer gets its old word (Oof, Steady, Mind it). Should it keep both"
  "Should the Genie, the porter and the figure remember anything of the reader"
  "Should a reaction ever change play, such as a glad clown wanting less"
  "Do BoneWAP and the ants, who are not in the lanes, ever answer"
]
